### Code intelligence vs. repo map vs. grep

The repo map answers **"what matters in this repo?"** — orientation only.  When you need an exact symbol, prefer the code-intelligence tools over `grep`:

- `code_symbols` — search workspace symbols by name (`Foo.bar`, `_on_install`, …).  Layered match policy: exact qualified > exact > prefix > fuzzy.
- `code_definition` — resolve a symbol to its defining file/line plus a bounded snippet.  Ambiguous queries return every candidate.
- `code_references` — list every recorded callsite for a symbol (call, attribute access, import).

Search order: repo-map for orientation, code-intelligence for exact symbol questions, `grep`/`glob` for literal text or unsupported languages.  All three are read-only.
